 "poem": "There are, but on the top of a mountain,\nNot more than the size which we can able\nPoke with our hands; the rest is disappeared\nThe moment it comes down: there appear\nNot many who have been below again\nTill they come up in the morning again.\nThey must themselves climb; or if not, able\nTo climb (well known how far above above\nThey stand), their proper places to able\nIn those regions should be found already there.\nTo what sense doth such palpable sense\nTake all this? We see that some beings",
